<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    RAZORJACK_IDENTITY_RESTYLE_1 — owner 2026-09-14: "Our razorjack looks
    strange to me. like a lava beast. It should not. It should look
    semi-camoulflaged with the tall grasses, like a predator might. Underside
    can be red, but above should be the same yellow-gold as the grasses.
    Needs regenerated description into our own modspace and a new Star
    Wars-esque name generated." Name picked by owner card the same day:
    SYTHECLAW.

    defName stays AA_Razorjack permanently — that ThingDef/PawnKindDef is
    still owned and shipped by the donor mod (sarg.alphaanimals), not
    absorbed into our own src/ tree, so it is not "ours" to rename under
    the three-tier scheme (NAMING_SCHEME_PLAN.md §1: the scheme governs our
    own shipping identity; a donor def only gets a new defName via a full
    vendored-absorption, like Armoury's, with a documented old->new map —
    not applicable here). This patch moves only the player-facing identity
    (labels + description) into our modspace. The art restyle (yellow-gold
    grass camo above, red underside) rides the same item through artpipe,
    no reference=.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Alpha Animals</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Razorjack"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>sytheclaw</label></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Razorjack"]/description</xpath>
          <value><description>A low-slung pack predator built for the tall gold grass of the burning plains. Above, its plates are the same dry yellow-gold as the standing quickgrass, so a hunting sytheclaw is a ripple in the field and nothing more; below, its underside is a raw furnace red that the prey only sees late. It trails the fire fronts the way other things trail water, taking whatever the smoke pushes out of cover, and its serrated forelimb blades leave a wound that ash gets into and keeps.</description></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="AA_Razorjack"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>sytheclaw</label></value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
